title: APT29 Mobile Watering-Hole Delivery Domains
id: 9c4b7e02-51a8-4f36-8d0e-b3f17a6c2e58
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects DNS/HTTP resolution of the delivery hostnames reported in the
    APT29 (Cozy Bear) mobile watering-hole campaign, which compromised
    legitimate websites and the Ukrainian analytics tracker Plerdy to
    fingerprint iOS and Android visitors and serve n-day exploit chains
    (CVE-2025-43529, CVE-2024-27834, CVE-2026-20700, CVE-2026-3910 and
    related flaws). A hit from a mobile user agent means the device was
    steered toward an exploit chain, not that the chain succeeded.
references:
    - https://www.darkreading.com/mobile-security/apt29-watering-holes-target-mobile-users
    - https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/apt29-linked-hackers-hijack-web.html
    - https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2026/11/04/apt29-watering-hole-mobile-devices-n-day-exploits/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/07
tags:
    - attack.t1189
    - attack.t1203
    - attack.t1608
logsource:
    category: network_connection
detection:
    selection_host:
        DestinationHostname|endswith:
            - 'theowo.club'
            - 'flux-telemetry.com'
            - 'america250.holiday'
            - 'adsprism-stat.com'
    condition: selection_host
falsepositives:
    - Sinkhole or research environments that replay the reported infrastructure
    - Legitimate domains that later fall under the same registrable names after the campaign takedown
level: high
